    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let the number of times Terrell must lift two 15-pound weights be x.\nIf Terrell lifts two 20-pound weights 12 times, he will lift a total of 20*12=240 pounds.\nIf Terrell lifts two 15-pound weights x times, he will lift a total of 15*2x=30x pounds.\nIn order to lift the same total weight, we need to have 30x=240.\nDividing both sides of the equation by 30 gives us x=8.\nTherefore, Terrell must lift two 15-pound weights 8 times in order to lift the same total weight as when he lifts two 20-pound weights 12 times.\nThe answer is: 8",
